  "source": "[\\pair:of{x, y}]\nDefines: p := \\set:of{\\set:of{x}, \\set:of{x, y}} is \\set\nwhen: x, y is \\\\anything\nDocumented:\n. called: \"pair of $x?$ and $y?$\"\n. written: \"\\langle x?, y? \\rangle\"\n. description: \"The ordered pair $\\langle x, y \\rangle$, encoded as the set\n                $\\{\\{x\\}, \\{x, y\\}\\}$. This encoding lets the first and second\n                components be recovered from the set alone, so order is\n                meaningful even though sets are unordered.\"\nId: \"8fd9d494-2882-4639-bb50-44a56626d1c4\"",
